---
import "../../nta.css";
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <title>NTA layout prototype</title>
  </head>

  <body>
    <main class="nta-page">
      <header class="nta-header">
        <div class="nta-header-text">
          <strong>U.S. Department of Homeland Security</strong>
          <strong>Notice to Appear</strong>
        </div>
        <div class="nta-double-rule" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="nta-rule-thick"></div>
          <div class="nta-rule-thin"></div>
        </div>
      </header>

      <section class="nta-content">
        <h1>
          In removal proceedings blah blah Immigration and Nationality Act:
        </h1>

        <div class="nta-identifiers nta-entered-data">
          <span>Subject ID:</span>
          <span>A#:</span>
          <span>DOB:</span>
        </div>

        <section class="nta-matter">
          <p>In the matter of:</p>

          <div class="nta-respondent">
            <div class="nta-form-text">
              Respondent:
              <span class="nta-blank"></span>
              who lives at:
            </div>

            <div class="nta-entered-data">
              123 anywhere st., apt 456, nowheresville, KS, 12345
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="nta-status-options">
          <div class="nta-checkbox-row">
            <span class="nta-checkbox" aria-hidden="true">
              □
            </span>
            <span>1. You are an arriving alien</span>
          </div>

          <div class="nta-checkbox-row">
            <span class="nta-checkbox" aria-hidden="true">
              □
            </span>
            <span>2. Blah blah admitted or paroled</span>
          </div>

          <div class="nta-checkbox-row">
            <span class="nta-checkbox" aria-hidden="true">
              □
            </span>
            <span>3. Yeah you can come in ughhhhh</span>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="nta-allegations">
          <p class="nta-form-text">
            The Department of Homeland Security alleges that you:
          </p>

          <ol class="nta-entered-data">
            <li>You are not a citizen or national of the United States</li>
            <li>You are a native of WAKANDA and a citizen of WAKANDA</li>
            <li>
              You entered into the United States at or near Paso del Norte
              Bridge in El Paso Texas, on or about January 1, 2000;
            </li>
            <li>
              You were not then admitted or paroled after inspection by an
              Immigration or Customs and Border Patrol official.
            </li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <section class="nta-charge">
          <p class="nta-form-text">
            Based on all that cattywampus hooey, you are subject to removal from
            the United States because of this jibberjabber:
          </p>

          <p class="nta-entered-data">
            212(a) (6) (A) (i) of the Immigration and Nationality Act, because
            we didn’t say you could come in, and we don’t even know where you
            came in or when you got here, and we totally did not give you
            permission or invite you.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="nta-review-options">
          <div class="nta-checkbox-row">
            <span class="nta-checkbox" aria-hidden="true">
              □
            </span>
            <span>Asylum officer credible fear review blah blah</span>
          </div>

          <div class="nta-checkbox-row">
            <span class="nta-checkbox" aria-hidden="true">
              □
            </span>
            <span>Absolute insane bullshit</span>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="nta-order">
          <p class="nta-form-text">
            <strong>YOU ARE ORDERED</strong> to appear before an immigration
            judge of the US DOJ at:
          </p>

          <p class="nta-entered-data">
            SOME RANDOM IMMIGRATION COURT 123 Main St., Hometownville KANSAS US
            12345
          </p>
          <div>
            <br />
            <p class="nta-entered-data">Ordinary government-machine text.</p>

            <p class="nta-entered-data nta-entered-data--vintage">
              This has been photocopied since the Clinton administration.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="nta-appearance-date">
            <span class="nta-form-text">On</span>
            <span class="nta-blank nta-date-blank"></span>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
